  "body": "Side branch: side/path-kernel\n\nSub-PR of the path kernel (#4023), K4b. Writer record: https://github.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/issues/4241#issuecomment-7206326747\n\n## The rule\n\nA link sample can stand in the cutter-centre area, in the air, or in the edge band. The edge band is the band outside the stock within one tool radius of a stock edge. The link stage reads it from the legal room of the entry stage (`entry::legal_room`, K5). There is no second definition.\n\nA sample in the edge band must also:\n- not be inside the part zone (the part grown by the tool radius plus the stock to leave), so that the disc meets no part;\n- be more than a tool radius from each keep-out area (else `HITS_FIXTURE`).\n\nThe part of the disc inside the stock is stock as any other. The swath test of K4 does not change: a sample that is not in the air must be within 0.9 tool radius of a cut already made (else `UNCUT_STOCK`). The old meaning \"outside the stock by 0.1 r counts as air\" is not ported.\n\n## What changed\n\n- `crates/pathkernel/src/link/proof.rs`: the chord proof accepts a sample in the edge band (`in_band`). The legal room is built once for each proof, at the first sample outside the centre area and the air.\n- `crates/pathkernel/src/link/route.rs`: the edge route also walks along the loops of the air: out through the band, along the air, back in. Each chord is proved as before.\n- `crates/pathkernel/src/region.rs`, `region_build.rs`: an `Outside` region keeps its part zone (`part_zone`, set by the builder only). The air now leaves out the part zone. Before, a part that reaches out of the stock was in the air, and the proof accepted a link in the air across it.\n- `crates/pathkernel/src/entry/room.rs`, `entry/mod.rs`: `legal_room` is `pub(crate)`, so that the link stage reads the same room.\n- The link law (`tests/laws/link_rule.rs`, `check_link`) reads the edge band too, from the stock of the case and not from the kernel's room.\n\nNo old planner changes. With the default switch the output is identical. The kernel still depends only on `camcraft-geometry`. The plan's transition table and the link stage stay the single gates.\n\n## Pins\n\nNegative first (`crates/pathkernel/tests/laws/link_rule.rs`):\n- `a_link_in_the_edge_band_over_uncut_stock_is_refused`: `UNCUT_STOCK`.\n- `a_link_in_the_edge_band_near_a_keep_out_is_refused`: `HITS_FIXTURE` (a clamp outside the stock).\n- `a_link_beside_a_part_that_reaches_out_of_the_stock_is_refused`: `CUTS_PART`; also no stay link across the part in the air.\n\nPositive:\n- `a_link_leaves_a_cut_at_the_stock_edge_runs_in_the_air_and_comes_back_over_cleared_stock`: stays at depth through the air. Without the cut made at the next start, the same link is refused with `UNCUT_STOCK`.\n\n## Counts before and after (measured again, no constant changed)\n\nLaw suite `order_link::k4_link_rule_holds_and_each_lift_is_named` (Auto / Inside / Outside) and motion pin `kernel_order_and_link_round_the_disc_and_the_dog_bone` (lifts, crossing feeds):\n\n| Fixture | Before | After |\n|---|---|---|\n| disc pocket (law suite) | 0 / 0 / 0 | 0 / 0 / 0 |\n| disc band (law suite) | 13 / 0 / 13 | 13 / 0 / 13 |\n| dog-bone band (law suite) | 15 / 0 / 15 | 15 / 0 / 15 |\n| pocket with an island (law suite) | 7 / 7 / 5 | 7 / 7 / 5 |\n| disc Inside (motion) | 0 lifts, 0 crossings | 0 lifts, 0 crossings |\n| disc Outside (motion) | 13 lifts, 0 crossings | 13 lifts, 0 crossings |\n| dog bone Inside (motion) | 0 lifts, 0 crossings | 0 lifts, 0 crossings |\n| dog bone Outside (motion) | 15 lifts, 0 crossings | 15 lifts, 0 crossings |\n\nThe target of 0 lifts on the disc is not met. Each of the 13 lifts on the disc band (Outside) is at the start of a piece that no cut has touched yet. The way in to that start runs over stock that is not within the swath of a cut made:\n- 4 `UNCUT_STOCK`: in a corner, from piece k on the long edge to piece k - 1 on the short edge. The next start is 4.4 mm or more from each cut made (the swath is 3.6 mm).\n- 4 `CUTS_PART`: from piece k (k = 7, 6) on one long edge to piece k - 1 on the other long edge. The straight link crosses the part; back along the cut, the next start is 3.98 mm and 5.47 mm from the cut made.\n- 5 `CROSSES_CUT`: from the last piece of a group to the first piece of the next group. The straight link crosses cuts; the way round through the air is proved out and along the air, but not back in to the first piece of the new group.\n\nThe decision says which rule can remove these lifts (an approach from the air proved as a lead-in). That changes the link rule, so it is not done here.\n\n## Decision\n\n`docs/decisions/4241-kernel-link-edge-band.md`.\n\n## Gate (final head)\n\n- `cargo check --tests -p camcraft-pathkernel`: pass.\n- `cargo check --tests -p camcraft-motion`: pass.\n- `camcraft-pathkernel` `laws` suite: 129 passed.\n- `camcraft-motion` `kernel_laws` suite: 29 passed.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-pathkernel -p camcraft-motion --all-targets -- -D warnings`: pass.\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/side/path-kernel`: pass, 4 steps (pathkernel lib, pathkernel `laws`, motion `kernel_laws` `k4_order_link::`), 0 failed, 0 stalled\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The light lane and the heavy lanes (no planner calls the kernel; a P7 PR runs no heavy step).\n- The `example_catalog*` suites: no post and no old toolpath changed.\n- A stock with more than one outline loop. The part zone covers it by construction, but no fixture has one.\n- The entry stage with a part that reaches out of the stock: its air room gets smaller there, and no entry pin has such a part.\n\nEffort: max\n\nChangelog: none\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nRefs #4241\n",
